--------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE GEMMA LANGUAGE MODEL — WHICH THE WORK DOES NOT SHIP
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Work contains no machine-learning model weights, and no copy of Gemma is
distributed with it.

The Work can optionally use Google's Gemma model ("Gemma") to write some of
its text while you play, locally on your own machine. If — and only if — you
turn that feature on, the Work downloads one copy of Gemma from a third-party
repository (huggingface.co) onto your own computer, at your request and for
you. The copyright holder of the Work does not supply, host or distribute
Gemma, and the game works fully without it: the hand-written text is there
and stays there.

Gemma is NOT part of the Work and is NOT licensed under this license — not
before you download it, and not after, when the file sits in the game's own
folder on your disk. Gemma is provided under and subject to the Gemma Terms
of Use found at ai.google.dev/gemma/terms.

You become bound by those Terms through the act of downloading or using
Gemma (Gemma Terms of Use, preamble). That is why the Work shows you those
Terms, and asks you to accept them, BEFORE it downloads anything. Copies of
the Terms and of the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy travel with the Work, in the
"Licenze" folder next to the game and readable in Settings -> Legal notices.

Nothing in this license restricts, or is intended to restrict, any right you
have in Gemma under the Gemma Terms of Use. If this license and the Gemma
Terms of Use disagree as to Gemma, the Gemma Terms of Use prevail.

USE RESTRICTIONS (binding). As a condition of your use of the Work together
with Gemma, you must not use Gemma or any Model Derivative:
  - for the restricted uses set out in the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy at
    ai.google.dev/gemma/prohibited_use_policy; or
  - in violation of applicable laws and regulations.
This is not a redistribution term: the Work redistributes nothing. It is
here because the Gemma Prohibited Use Policy binds not only whoever uses
Gemma but also whoever "allow[s] others to use" it — and the Work is what
puts Gemma into your hands.

Google claims no rights in the text Gemma generates on your machine, and you
are solely responsible for that text and its subsequent use (Gemma Terms of
Use, Section 3.3). The copyright holder of the Work makes no warranty as to
generated text, which is produced on your device and is not reviewed by
anyone before you read it.

Gemma and Google are trademarks of Google LLC. The Work is not affiliated
with, sponsored by, or endorsed by Google; those names are used only to say
which model the Work can use.

THE WORK IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE COPYRIGHT HOLDER BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING FROM THE WORK OR ITS USE.

For permission requests, contact the copyright holder.

